    "updated_at": "2020-11-29T18:36:17Z",
    "body": "Whoa, that's weird.\r\n\r\nThe only guess I have is that LightDM is somehow trying to eval the contents of `.bashrc` with some sort of POSIX-compliance on, because that's what I see when running bash in POSIX mode:\r\n\r\n```\r\n12:33:49 ❯ bash --posix            \r\nbash-5.0$ eval \"$(starship init bash)\"\r\nbash: syntax error near unexpected token `('\r\nbash-5.0$ source <(\"/usr/bin/starship\" init bash --print-full-init)\r\nbash: syntax error near unexpected token `('\r\nbash-5.0$ \r\n```\r\n\r\nbut why this is happening or how to fix it I don't know.",
