    "created_at": "2023-03-23T12:50:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-23T12:50:21Z",
    "body": "I'm not sure about the specific case of LightDM, but Bash will turn on the POSIX mode when it is called via `/bin/sh`. The error here is caused because Bash < 5.1 does not allow process substitutions when it is in the POSIX mode. Instead of doing `source <(...)` or `source /dev/stdin <<< \"$(...)\"`, we can just use `eval -- \"$(...)\"`. Is there any reason we stick with the process substitution or do not use `eval`?\r\n\r\n",
